                <pb facs="0932" n="814" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg814"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6731/125: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-09T11:00:00+02:00">April 9, 1929—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 9—8:55 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>24. My 2, April 4, 5 p.m., from Angora. Exchange of notes putting into effect
                    commercial <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> between the United States
                    and Turkey for one year from April 11th, 1929, took place yesterday afternoon.
                    Customs authorities throughout Turkey telegraphically notified from Angora.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
